.docname {Installation}
.include {docs}

## Download a release

Every tagged release on the .repolink {GitHub Releases page} {releases} has ready-to-run builds, so you don't need a Rust toolchain. Download the archive for your platform, unpack it, and run `gol-bevy`.

Each archive has the binary, the README, the changelog, the licence, the font's licence (`OFL.txt`), and the licences of the crates compiled in (`THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.html`). The app needs nothing else on disk: built-in patterns and the UI font are embedded in the binary. Each release also lists the SHA-256 checksum of every archive in `SHA256SUMS`. To check a download, put both in one folder and run `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing`, or `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing` on macOS.

### Linux (x86_64)

Download the `x86_64-linux.tar.gz` archive. It needs:

- glibc 2.39 or newer (Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 13, Fedora 40, or later)
- a Wayland or X11 desktop
- for the file dialogs that open and save workspaces and \.rle files, an xdg-desktop-portal backend, such as `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk` or `xdg-desktop-portal-kde`

```shell
tar -xzf gol-bevy-<version>-x86_64-linux.tar.gz
./gol-bevy-<version>-x86_64-linux/gol-bevy
```

### Windows (x86_64)

Download the `x86_64-windows.zip` archive, unzip it, and run `gol-bevy.exe`. Release builds open no console window.

### macOS (universal)

The macOS archive runs natively on both Apple silicon and Intel Macs.

> Warning: The binary is not signed, so macOS blocks it the first time you open it.

Either allow it under **System Settings → Privacy & Security**, or clear the quarantine flag in the unpacked folder:

```shell
xattr -d com.apple.quarantine gol-bevy
```

## Run from source

If you have the repository checked out, run the app with Cargo:

```shell
cargo run
```

The first build takes a while, because dependencies are compiled with full optimization even in dev builds. See [Building from source](development.qd) for the pinned toolchain, the Linux system libraries, and faster rebuilds.

## Window and board size

The window opens at 1200 × 800 and can be resized down to 800 × 420. On first launch the board is sized to fill the window. After that, the board keeps the size you choose in [Settings](settings.qd), whatever the window size.

